    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d81">

                <pb facs="0252" n="207" sameAs="frus:frus1977-80v19/pg207"/>

                <head>81. Memorandum From Secretary of State Vance to President Carter<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d81-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1977-07-22">July 22, 1977</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>[Omitted here is material unrelated to India.]</p>
                <p>8. <hi rendition="#italic">India: Nuclear Question:</hi> With the Tarapur
                    shipment on the way, our nuclear discussions with India move into a more
                    intensive phase. Joe Nye will be in India with ACDA and ERDA colleagues August
                    1–3 and plans to follow up the points in your July 15 letter to Prime Minister
                        Desai.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d81-f2"/> In the meanwhile, Desai has publicly
                    declared his opposition to further testing, including PNE’s, and his stand has
                    triggered opposition criticism and the charge that he is bowing to U.S. pressure
                    to obtain fuel supplies for the Tarapur reactors.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d81-f3"/>
                    There has also been increased Indian press discussion of the comprehensive
                    safeguards issue and support for continued Indian opposition to accepting IAEA
                    safeguards on indigenously produced nuclear facilities.<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d81-f4"/> When pressed on this issue in parliament, Desai stated
                    only that he would never accept a discriminatory arrangement. Comprehensive
                    safeguards will be the main problem in our nuclear negotiations now that Desai
                    has ruled out further testing.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
